---
name: cesium-rule
description: This rule MUST be applied to all Cesium related code writing and refactoring.
---

# Constant Enum

When Cesium provides a constant enum, you MUST use the enum constant (e.g., `LabelStyle.FILL_AND_OUTLINE`) instead of the numeric value (e.g., `2`).

**Examples:**
- Good: `style: LabelStyle.FILL_AND_OUTLINE`
- Bad: `style: 2`

- Good: `horizontalOrigin: HorizontalOrigin.CENTER`
- Bad: `horizontalOrigin: 0`

- Good: `verticalOrigin: VerticalOrigin.TOP`
- Bad: `verticalOrigin: -1`

